      "writtenOn": "2025-04-07T16:29:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we change this to have 4 values like:\nkFixed \u003d 0b000, // Uses explicit `DrawWriter::draw` functions\nkAppendVertices \u003d 0b001, // Appends vertices\nkAppendInstances \u003d 0b010, // Appends instances with a static vertex count\nkAppendDynamicInstances \u003d 0b100, // Appends instances with flexible vertex count\n\nThere are two competing \"dynamic\" concepts at play with DrawWriter, so I think this helps differentiate them: 1. whether or not some type of data is being appended, so the draw count is dynamic, or 2. whether or not the instance\u0027s definition is itself dynamic.\n\nRight now no RenderStep will use kFixed, but there is a good chance that as we flesh out the implementation for the `SkMesh` and `SkVertices` APIs that we would cache GPU buffers associated with the user-facing objects.  In that case, the VerticesRenderStep would be kFixed and call the direct `draw` functions with BindBufferInfos from the mesh object.",
