      "writtenOn": "2025-04-07T16:29:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A lot of the original complexity in `setTemplate` was because it was trying to support implicit changes to render state flags at any point in time. Now, we know the render state flags are only changing in one place: `newPipelineState` and it already has a call to flush().\n\nsetTemplate only has to flush if the buffers are changing (rare), but could be a way to account for the pending base calculations instead of also having to reset them in newPipelineState. Something like:\n\n    uint32_t newPendingBaseVertex \u003d 0;\n    if (vertices.fBuffer) {\n        if (vertices.fOffset % fVertexStride \u003d\u003d 0) {\n            newPendingBaseVertex \u003d vertices.fOffset / fVertexStride;\n            vertices.fOffset \u003d 0;\n        } // else will have to bind directly to the original byte offset\n    } else {\n        // Vertices aren\u0027t used, so carry prior state forward so we don\u0027t change\n        // state that is ignored by the current pipeline.\n        vertices \u003d fVertices;\n        newPendingBaseVertex \u003d fPendingBaseVertex;\n    }\n    \n    // ... repeat for instances and matching fields and indices.\n    \n    // With `vertices` offset hopefully set to 0, this will hopefully be true rarely.\n    bool needBindingChange \u003d vertices !\u003d fVertices || instances !\u003d fInstances ...\n    bool pendingBaseChange \u003d newPendingBaseVertex !\u003d fPendingBaseVertices || ...\n    if (fPendingCount \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 (needBindingChange || pendingBaseChange)) {\n        this-\u003eflush();\n    }\n    \n    fPendingBufferBinds \u003d needBindingChange;\n    fVertices \u003d vertices;\n    fPendingBaseVertex \u003d newPendingBaseVertex;\n    // etc.\n    \nWith this logic for setting pending bases, I think we can just get rid of the pending base assignment in newPipelineState entirely because we will always have a later call to `setTemplate`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 42,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "bdd7f363515cbe8373627cbce411bcde7155c5fb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
