        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-07T17:56:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it keep things simpler if we handled the ARM padding in `newPipelineState`? If the old render state was vertices (regardless of if the new state was vertices or instances), a new pipeline means the end padding needs to be zero\u0027ed.\n\nBut all reserved excess bytes should be returned at this point, so we can have DrawWriter zero out bytes up to a multiple of (4*old vertex stride), right?",
      "parentUuid": "89cb7555_d53f0b5c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 118,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 118,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "bdd7f363515cbe8373627cbce411bcde7155c5fb",
