      "author": {
        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-07T18:45:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s doable---you do still have `fNextWriter` to zero out the bytes. The only problem is that you will need a `TakeBackBytes` function to make sure the pointers get updated and you don\u0027t stomp the padding on vertices-\u003einstance switch.\n\nI\u0027ll make the changes to this CL, assuming this works :).",
      "parentUuid": "d29fccc5_a01233de",
